wine-sg (10.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Run real Microsoft winget-cli under Wine (Stained Glass patches 0026-0027):
    - SHGetKnownFolderPath accepts KF_FLAG_NO_APPCONTAINER_REDIRECTION, which
      every packaged Microsoft app passes; rejecting it made winget throw
      through a noexcept boundary and die before printing (0026).
    - implement and register Windows.ApplicationModel.Core.CoreApplication with
      a working CoreApplication.Properties (a small IPropertySet), which winget
      activates at start-up (0027).
    With these, `winget --version' and `winget --help' run under wine-sg.

 -- Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 15:46:38 -0700

wine-sg (10.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Multi-user hardening and features (Stained Glass patches 0014-0025):
    - clients open/create/delete/rename/reopen/chmod files with their own Unix
      rights; per-user process agent for cross-uid ptrace/signal (D14/D16/D19).
    - only SYSTEM mints administrator tokens; owners open their own processes
      (D17/D18); per-user SID names (D12); USERPROFILE ordering (D15).
    - registry: enforce a key's DACL on subkey creation (S2 clause 3); read the
      graphics driver and machine Group Policy (SHRestricted) from HKLM.
    - "Run as administrator" routes to the elevation broker.

